# Rolls-Royce 25/30, 1936-1938.
#
# The 25/30 replaced the 20/25: 4,257 cc six, wheelbase 3,353 mm, overall
# dimensions body-dependent (about 5,080 x 1,830 x 1,700 mm as a saloon). About
# 1,201 chassis built before the Wraith succeeded it; the last of the small
# pre-war Rolls-Royces and a class-4 model of the late 1930s.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_25/30
#
# Colours: Black, Dark Green, Maroon and Grey are documented period finishes.
#
# Weight: 10 in total (black 4, green 3, maroon 2, grey 1).
#
# Speed 130 km/h; comfort 80/450 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1936-1938 with a road tail to about 1960.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-25-30.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rolls-royce-25-30/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RollsRoyce2530(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=4
intro_year=1936
intro_month=4
retire_year=1960
retire_month=6
speed=130
length=3
class=4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=450

